WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.544 --> 00:00:13.909
Nina stomped her boots on the floor.

2
00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:16.554
Her mom had forgotten to pack her sneakers.

3
00:00:16.555 --> 00:00:19.745
So she had to wear these hot boots all day.

4
00:00:19.746 --> 00:00:24.066
Nina's baby sister, Lulu, took up most of Mom's time now.

5
00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:28.323
"Baby first," her mom always said.

6
00:00:28.324 --> 00:00:33.670
"Nina, please join us for the craft," Miss Shelly said.

7
00:00:33.671 --> 00:00:37.569
Nina slowly walked over.

8
00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:41.573
The table was covered in orange, brown, and green.

9
00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:45.679
"It looks like a pumpkin patch!" Izzie said.

10
00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:50.062
"We're going to make yarn pumpkins," Miss Shelly said.

11
00:00:50.063 --> 00:00:52.459
"Everyone will work with a partner.

12
00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:57.779
The pumpkins have to dry overnight, so it will take two days.

13
00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:01.001
Bobby, I'll work with you."

14
00:01:01.002 --> 00:01:03.737
Izzie and Jason were partners.

15
00:01:03.738 --> 00:01:07.141
Ethan looked at Nina. "Want to be partners?"

16
00:01:07.142 --> 00:01:12.996
Nina blushed. "Okay." She looked at the instructions.

17
00:01:12.997 --> 00:01:16.662
"First, blow up a balloon about halfway.

18
00:01:16.663 --> 00:01:19.534
This will be the size of your pumpkin."

19
00:01:19.535 --> 00:01:23.275
Nina blew up her balloon halfway.

20
00:01:23.276 --> 00:01:28.805
"Tie a piece of yarn to the balloon and hang it from a stick," Ethan said.

21
00:01:28.806 --> 00:01:33.136
Nina tied the string while Ethan held the stick.

22
00:01:33.137 --> 00:01:40.227
"Great. Now dunk one string of yarn into your glue bowl," Miss Shelly said.

23
00:01:40.228 --> 00:01:44.434
"You can use a plastic fork to help with the dipping."

24
00:01:44.435 --> 00:01:47.921
Nina gently slid the yarn through the plastic fork.

25
00:01:47.922 --> 00:01:53.347
She giggled as she dipped. "This part is fun!"

26
00:01:53.348 --> 00:01:56.150
"One partner holds the stick.

27
00:01:56.151 --> 00:02:00.096
The other wraps the yarn around the balloon.

28
00:02:00.097 --> 00:02:04.729
Carefully press the yarns' ends down on the balloon.

29
00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:07.977
They must stick," Miss Shelly said.

30
00:02:07.978 --> 00:02:10.377
Nina dipped more yarn into glue.

31
00:02:10.378 --> 00:02:14.035
"Now we repeat the steps one more time," Ethan said.

32
00:02:14.036 --> 00:02:18.032
"You can make a few more pumpkins," Miss Shelly said.

33
00:02:18.033 --> 00:02:20.832
"The pumpkins must dry overnight.

34
00:02:20.833 --> 00:02:23.651
So we'll finish them tomorrow."

35
00:02:23.652 --> 00:02:28.464
"I want to make four pumpkins," Nina said.

36
00:02:28.465 --> 00:02:31.743
She blew up two larger balloons.

37
00:02:31.744 --> 00:02:38.605
Then she blew up one very small balloon.

38
00:02:38.606 --> 00:02:42.297
Finally everyone set their sticks on the table.

39
00:02:42.298 --> 00:02:46.704
The pumpkins had to dry.

40
00:02:46.705 --> 00:02:50.360
The next day Izzie pointed to Nina's dried balloons.

41
00:02:50.361 --> 00:02:53.773
"A baby pumpkin! Cute!"

42
00:02:53.774 --> 00:02:56.858
"Is that baby Lulu?" Jason asked.

43
00:02:56.859 --> 00:03:00.798
Nina was surprised. "You can tell?"

44
00:03:00.799 --> 00:03:10.253
"No, I mean, is that baby Lulu?" Jason pointed to the gym door.

45
00:03:10.254 --> 00:03:14.106
"Mom!" Nina jumped up.

46
00:03:14.107 --> 00:03:18.348
"Shh, she fell asleep," Nina's mom whispered.

47
00:03:18.349 --> 00:03:21.687
"So I decided to pick you up early."

48
00:03:21.688 --> 00:03:26.683
"Does that mean you can help me with my craft?" Nina asked hopefully.

49
00:03:26.684 --> 00:03:30.261
"Yes!"

50
00:03:30.262 --> 00:03:32.835
Nina showed her the four pumpkins.

51
00:03:32.836 --> 00:03:37.894
"What a beautiful family of pumpkins," Nina's mom said.

52
00:03:37.895 --> 00:03:41.224
"It's our family," Nina said.

53
00:03:41.225 --> 00:03:46.308
Miss Shelly showed everyone how to push on the dry balloons to release them from the yarn.

54
00:03:46.309 --> 00:03:50.124
Next they cut a hole at the top to let out the air.

55
00:03:50.125 --> 00:03:54.971
Then they pulled out the balloons.

56
00:03:54.972 --> 00:03:59.741
"Now make vines and a stem," Miss Shelly said.

57
00:03:59.742 --> 00:04:06.566
Izzie wrapped a green pipe cleaner around each pointer finger. "Curly vines!"

58
00:04:06.567 --> 00:04:09.901
Nina and her mom picked up their pipe cleaners.

59
00:04:09.902 --> 00:04:13.530
Just then baby Lulu let out a cry.

60
00:04:13.531 --> 00:04:17.438
Nina's mom rushed over.

61
00:04:17.439 --> 00:04:27.802
Nina smiled. "I guess I'll finish my pumpkins at home. Baby first!"
